        <body>
            <div xml:id="d880">

                <pb facs="0933" n="813" xml:id="pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Bandit Activities, 1931/43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Bluefields</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rowe</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-18T16:00:00-05:45">April 18, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>In view of repeated rumors of threatened bandit attack upon El Gallo, the Fruit
                    Company Station, 3 officers and 27 enlisted Guardia are being sent there,
                    leaving 3 officers and 13 Guardia in Bluefields. One officer and 30 enlisted
                    Marines from U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Sacramento</hi> are being landed at
                    Bluefields today to assure order in the absence of Guardia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rowe</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
